{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790192138,"nonce":"3F512v4uMOXrf8LHAorCZdQNr74=","message":"Revised 2026-09-23 (Luis): there is no view entity and no view new|patch|rm. Rendering is the `view` module and command, an atomic capability git-work provides: `view.board(items, columns=...)`, `view.gantt(items, start=..., end=..., group_by=...)`, `view.list(items, ...)` build a spec from items plus field bindings named by the caller; renderers consume specs. CLI form: `git work view board '{\"columns\":\"status\"}' \u003c items.json`, TTY opens the interactive view, otherwise prints the spec, `--gui` sends it to the browser. A saved view is a flow whose function returns a spec (f37603c). A view that edits (kanban drag) calls issue.set and re-renders. Rules are gone with automation (47b8430). Full map: doc/design/cli-convention.md.","files":null}]}